          'Present simple passive: is / are + p.p. → English is spoken all over the world.',
          'Past simple passive: was / were + p.p. → The restaurant was built in 1916.',
          'With modals: can be / cannot be + p.p. → It cannot be immediately explained.',
          'After another verb we use "to be + p.p." → Movies started to be made.',
